source_corpus.comment:4328609849:
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The logic to check if the technology has any unidirectional routing layers is duplicated in both `FlexDR::searchRepair` and `FlexDR::main`. Extracting this into an idiomatic C++ lambda makes the variable `const` and improves maintainability.

```c
  const bool has_unidir_layer = [this]() {
    for (const auto& layer : getTech()->getLayers()) {
      if (layer->getType() == dbTechLayerType::ROUTING
          && layer->isUnidirectional()) {
        return true;
      }
    }
    return false;
  }();
```

