Calling `history_args.back()` without checking if `history_args` is empty can lead to undefined behavior. It is safer to check `!history_args.empty()` first.

```c
    if (!history_args.empty() && drvs > prev_drvs && history_args.back().ripupMode == RipUpMode::NEARDRC) {
      const int settle_size = std::max(7, history_args.back().size);
```

